The #19 branch is pushed and the PR is open: [#21](https://github.com/NatsumeRyuhane/qingci-test/pull/21), `feat(contracts)!: 知识库契约、带状态的时间与角色证据`, with `Closes #19`. The branch was already up to date with `main`, so the 10 signed commits went up as they were.

**The PR description covers:**
- one row per commit;
- the checks I ran and their results;
- the real-data before/after: `replied` 2,166 → 1,303 and `undetermined` 139 → 1,002;
- the two breaking schema bumps. Re-running `copilot ingest` replaces the old cases file, and reading the old file fails with a clear version error.

The choices I made that the issue didn't specify are listed for review:
- the Notice event window is kept separate from its validity window;
- policies match fixed phrases instead of regexes;
- the repetition threshold is a code parameter;
- `Draft.time_context` stays optional;
- only `Case.id`, thread IDs and message IDs are restricted, not references to cases elsewhere;
- system-mail structure counts as strong evidence.

It also restates that all fixtures are synthetic and repeats the accepted risk of forged quote headers.

I won't poll for reviews; tell me when they're in. Once #21 merges, #5 can start against these contracts.
